      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T09:38:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for reviewing. \n\nI\u0027ve considered about this. All the other messages will be deferred except CMD_REEVALUATE. That is, to say, NetworkMonitor will stop and wait until we get the CMD_PROBE_COMPLETE which is quite similar to previous behavior. And CMD_REEVALUATE is currently sent when \n1. The validation fail(which is triggered after CMD_PROBE_COMPLETE).\n2. The enter() of EvaluatingState\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000. \nSince the state will not leave EvaluatingState\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000, it should not have change to re-enter EvaluatingState\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000. \n\nThus, this condition should not happen in current design. Of course, the the sequence is updated in the future. It might happen.",
      "parentUuid": "72819bcc_58b9e27c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 849,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 849,
        "endChar": 40
