      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T10:21:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion over IM: I think you\u0027re probably right that this cannot happen. I think it\u0027s a bit brittle, because correctness depends on a number of invariants of the code outside this state. So if we make a simple change code outside this state, the code in this state could become incorrect without us noticing.\n\nSo I think we should at least have a comment here that says something like:\n\n  // If we get here, the probe started in enter() is guaranteed to have completed, because\n  // in this state, all messages except CMD_PROBE_COMPLETE and CMD_REEVALUATE\n  // are deferred. CMD_REEVALUATE cannot be in the queue, because it is only ever sent in\n  // EvaluatingState#enter, and we reach this state by processing it. Therefore there is\n  // no need to stop the thread.",
      "parentUuid": "8cdd6d2f_720cb209",
